A rule that affects how an attributed string performs automatic grammatical agreement.

Use an inflection rule to add grammatical agreement to a localized string.
To do this, set the ``InflectionRule`` attribute on an attributed string,
then call the `inflected()` method on the attributed string.

For example, the following code creates an attributed string that uses
automatic grammatical agreement:

```swift
func attributedText(for food: String) -> AttributedString {
    var string = AttributedString(localized: "\(food) was added to your order.")
    string.inflect = InflectionRule.automatic
    return string.inflected()
}
```

